  "body_html": "<p><a href=\"../../qei-foundation/donate/index.html\"><img alt='Heading text: \"Spring Microplate Reader Appeal\"' class=\"aligncenter wp-image-6035 size-full\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"250\" id=\"longdesc-return-6035\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=6035&amp;referrer=6085\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Appeal-heading-1.png\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Appeal-heading-1.png 600w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Appeal-heading-1-300x125.png 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Appeal-heading-1-400x167.png 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"600\"/></a></p>\n<p>The Queensland Eye Institute (QEI) Foundation has funded vision research for more than 60 years, working to eradicate preventable blindness.</p>\n<p>This spring the QEI Foundation is running a special appeal to replace a <strong>Microplate Reader</strong>, equipment that detects and quantifies chemical, biological, or physical reactions or properties within the wells of a microplate. This equipment is essential for efficient screening in research, diagnostics, and drug discovery.</p>\n<p>The system in QEI’s laboratory has failed beyond repair and replacing it is now a priority.  Our scientists are facing significant delays, relying on a rented machine when possible, or travelling to other labs to complete their work.</p>\n<p>Throughout September, October and November, every donation made to the QEI Foundation will go directly towards purchasing a new microplate reader system.</p>\n<p><a href=\"../../qei-foundation/donate/index.html\">Click here to donate</a></p>\n<figure aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5988\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\" id=\"attachment_5988\" style=\"width: 640px\"><img alt=\"A young man with curly hair looks through a microscope. A computer monitor beside him has images of cells.\" class=\"wpa-warning wpa-suspicious-alt size-large wp-image-5988\" data-warning=\"Suspicious alt text\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"427\" id=\"longdesc-return-5988\" longdesc=\"https://qei.org.au?longdesc=5988&amp;referrer=6085\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\" src=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-1024x683.jpg\" srcset=\"../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-1024x683.jpg 1024w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-300x200.jpg 300w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-768x512.jpg 768w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-2048x1366.jpg 2048w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-1430x954.jpg 1430w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-800x533.jpg 800w, ../../wp-content/uploads/2025/08/20250724_QEI-silk-sericin-research-16_Web-400x267.jpg 400w\" tabindex=\"-1\" width=\"640\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text\" id=\"caption-attachment-5988\">A tissue culture plate is used to compare cell cultures grown with and without a sericin gel base.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Read about QEI’s silk sericin research, which relies on a microplate reader, <a href=\"../how-the-humble-silkworm-might-help-save-sight/index.html\">at this link</a>.</p>",
